{title: 187 - Jesus, What a Friend for Sinners}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #187 • HOLY MANNA • 8.7.8.9}
{lyricist: J. Wilbur Chapman}
{composer: Wm. Moore's Columbian Harmony}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 187}
{meta: tune HOLY MANNA}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.9}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus! [Dm/A]what [F]a [Am]Friend for [Bb]sinners!
[F]Jesus! Lover ofmy soul;
[F]Friends may fail [Gm/Bb]me, foes assail [Dm/A]me,
[Am]He, [Gm]my Savior, [F]makes me whole.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Hallelujah! what a [Gm/Bb]Savior!
[F/C]Hallelujah! [C7]what a [D7]Friend!
[F/C]Saving, helping, [Dm/A]keeping, [C]loving,
[Am]He is [F]with me to the [C/E]end.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Jesus! [Dm/A]what [F]a [Am]Strength in [Bb]weakness!
[F]Let me hide myself in Him.
[F]Tempted, tried, and [Gm/Bb]sometimes [Dm/A]failing,
[Am]He, [Gm]my [Dm/A]Strength, my [F]victory wins.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Jesus! [Dm/A]what [F]a [Am]Help in [Bb]sorrow!
[F]While the billows over me roll,
[F]Even when [Gm/Bb]my heart is [Dm/A]breaking,
[Am]He, [Gm]my [Dm/A]Comfort, [F]helps my soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Jesus! [Dm/A]I [F]do [Am]now receive [Bb]Him,
[F]Jesus! I do now adore Him,]
[F]More than all [Gm/Bb]in Him [Dm/A]I find.
[F]He hath granted [Gm/Bb]me forgiveness,
[Am]I [Gm]am [Dm/A]His, [F]and He is mine.
{end_of_verse}
